    "snippet": "⭐ 1/5 — BUYER BEWARE: Great Scooter, Terrible Ownership Experience\nThe Ola S1 Pro looks futuristic, rides well and is packed with technology. Unfortunately, the real problem starts after you buy it.\nOla’s after-sales service has been extremely frustrating. Getting a service appointment is a challenge, issues take too long to get addressed, and customer support often leaves you chasing for answers.\nI even paid for Ola Care Plus — supposedly for peace of mind. Instead, it felt like money thrown away. What is the value of a service plan when getting basic service itself becomes a struggle?\nAnd the final punchline: after 4 years of ownership, my “future of mobility” is now being SCRAPPED.\nThat SCRAPPED stamp on the scooter says more about my ownership experience than any Ola advertisement ever could.\nGreat technology means nothing without dependable after-sales support.\nOla needs to understand one simple thing: selling a scooter is not the end of the customer relationship — it’s the beginning.\nS1 Pro: ⭐ 1/5\nTechnology: Impressive\nAfter-sales service: Extremely disappointing\nOla Care Plus: Money wasted, based on my experience\nOwnership experience: Deeply frustrating",
    "extracted_snippet": {
     "original": "⭐ 1/5 — BUYER BEWARE: Great Scooter, Terrible Ownership Experience\nThe Ola S1 Pro looks futuristic, rides well and is packed with technology. Unfortunately, the real problem starts after you buy it.\nOla’s after-sales service has been extremely frustrating. Getting a service appointment is a challenge, issues take too long to get addressed, and customer support often leaves you chasing for answers.\nI even paid for Ola Care Plus — supposedly for peace of mind. Instead, it felt like money thrown away. What is the value of a service plan when getting basic service itself becomes a struggle?\nAnd the final punchline: after 4 years of ownership, my “future of mobility” is now being SCRAPPED.\nThat SCRAPPED stamp on the scooter says more about my ownership experience than any Ola advertisement ever could.\nGreat technology means nothing without dependable after-sales support.\nOla needs to understand one simple thing: selling a scooter is not the end of the customer relationship — it’s the beginning.\nS1 Pro: ⭐ 1/5\nTechnology: Impressive\nAfter-sales service: Extremely disappointing\nOla Care Plus: Money wasted, based on my experience\nOwnership experience: Deeply frustrating"
